    <DataNode elementId="AT4G35830-MONOMER" textLabel="Aconitate hydratase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G35830-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="675" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">ACO1 is an aconitase that can catalyze the conversion of |FRAME: CIT| to |FRAME: THREO-DS-ISO-CITRATE| through a |FRAME: CIS-ACONITATE| intermediate, based on the phenotype of reduced aconitase activity in an &lt;i&gt;aco1&lt;/i&gt; mutant |CITS: [17013749]|. ACO1 may participate in the TCA cycle and other primary metabolic pathways and it is believed to accumulate in the mitochondria and the cytosol |CITS: [17013749]|. Interestingly, ACO1 can specifically bind to the 5&apos; UTR of |FRAME: AT2G28190|, which encodes a superoxide dismutase, &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and can affect the levels of |FRAME: AT2G28190| transcript accumulation &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;. Either through this mechanism or other undiscovered mechanisms, ACO1 appears to play a role in the response to oxidative stress in Arabidopsis thaliana |CITS: [17013749]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G35830-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Aconitase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Citrate hydro-lyase 1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33458, RXN-33457, RXN-T9-2104, RXN-5978" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G35830.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G35830" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17013749" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G53240-MONOMER" textLabel="Malate dehydrogenase 1, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZP06" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="675" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">mMDH1 is one of two mitochondrial malate dehydrogenases in Arabidopsis thaliana, based on a mutant analysis that shows a 30% reduction in total leaf malate dehydrogenase activity in &lt;i&gt;mmdh1-2 &lt;/i&gt; mutants. In addition, an &lt;i&gt;mmdh1-2 mmdh2-1&lt;/i&gt; double mutant has 40% lower levels of leaf malate dehydrogenase activity suggesting that both mMDH1 and mMDH2 are active malate dehydrogenases in Arabidopsis |CITS: [20876337]|. The larger contribution of mMDH1 to the malate dehydrogenase activity is consistent with it being the major isoform found in mitochondria according to proteomic analyses |CITS: [18385124][11743115]|. The activity of this enzyme was additionally demonstrated when reintroduction of 35S:mMDH1 into the double mutant restored whole leaf malate dehydrogenase activity |CITS: [20876337]|. The exclusive mitochondrial localization of these two MDH family members is further supported by the observation that&lt;i&gt;mmdh1-2 mmdh2-1&lt;/i&gt; double mutants have no detectable mitochondrial malate dehydrogenase activity |CITS: [20876337]|. They have several other abnormalities, such as slow growth, reduced mitochondrial oxidation, and reduced net carbon dioxide assimilation |CITS: [20876337]|. Some aspects of the &lt;i&gt;mmdh1-2 mmdh2-1&lt;/i&gt; double mutant&apos;s phenotype indicate that the mMDHs in Arabidopsis may act primarily on OAA to promote malate formation &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;|CITS: [20876337]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G53240-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G53240.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR016040" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9ZP06" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9ZP06" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00056" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phylomedb" value="Q9ZP06" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS00068" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11540" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9ZP06" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Mitochondrial MDH1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="mMDH1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="Mitochondrial NAD-dependent malate dehydrogenase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="mNAD-MDH 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_5" value="mtNAD-MDH1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-7084" />
